  "result": "Done! I've added payment terms support to the invoicing system. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Updated `src/invoices.js`\n\n- **Payment terms support in `createInvoice()`**:\n  - Accepts optional `terms` parameter: `'NET14'`, `'NET30'` (default), or `'EOM'`\n  - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on the returned invoice\n  - Returns `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n\n- **Helper functions**:\n  - `lastDayOfMonth(dateStr)` \u2014 Calculates the last day of the month for EOM terms\n  - `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` \u2014 Maps terms to due date calculations:\n    - NET14: 14 days from issue date\n    - NET30: 30 days from issue date\n    - EOM: Last day of the issue date's month\n\n## Updated `src/errors.js`\n\nAdded error code:\n- `TERMS_INVALID` \u2014 Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM.\n\n## Added 8 tests to `test/invoices.test.js`\n\n- Default terms (NET30)\n- NET14 and NET30 explicit terms with correct due dates\n- EOM terms (works across different months, including leap years)\n- Invalid terms error cases (unknown term, empty string)\n- Terms preservation\n\n**All 162 tests pass** (8 new + 154 existing).",
